.\n\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\n1.  Create `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`.\n2.  Define the page's `metadata` object for the title.\n3.  Build the page component, importing and rendering `<Header />` and `<Footer />`.\n4.  Add a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag containing a valid `FAQPage` schema with 5 placeholder questions and answers about Singapore-JB visa runs.\n5.  Add a second `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag for the `HowTo` schema, detailing a 5-step process for a visa run.\n6.  Include a clear Call-to-Action (CTA) button or link pointing to `/book`.\n7.  Edit `site/src/app/sitemap.ts` to add an entry for `/visa-run` with a `priority` of `0.85`.\n\n**4. Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\n*   Ensure the JSON-LD content is valid and passes schema validation tools.\n*   The content for the FAQ and How-To steps must be generated, as it's not in the story. It should be relevant and high-quality.\n*   Verify the correct import path for the `<Footer />` component, as it may differ from the `<Header />` path.\n*   The final implementation must pass `npm run build` without errors.\n\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  4:42:42 AM\nFAILED diff-guard: New page: /visa-run — Dedicated Visa Run Resource Hub with FAQPage + HowTo Schema (ID: US-246) — 11574 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-246 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\nThis user story is for a Next.js/TypeScript project, not Frappe/Python. Here is the technical brief based on the provided JSON:\n\n**Project:** Next.js Website (pelangi-website)\n**User Story:** US-246: New page: /visa-run\n\n**1. Files to Modify:**\n*   **Create:** `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`\n*   **Modify:** `site/src/app/sitemap.ts`\n\n**2. Framework/Concepts Involved:**\n*   Next.js App Router: Creating a new route segment.\n*   React Server Component: The new page will be a Server Component.\n*   Next.js Metadata API: To set the page `<title>`.\n*   JSON-LD Schema: `FAQPage` and `HowTo` schemas for SEO.\n*   Sha