Malaysia (2026)\"\n*   **Step 4:** Write the post content as a string, following the description. It must be a step-by-step guide including vehicle requirements and the RM20-50/hour earnings estimate.\n*   **Step 5:** After implementation, run `npm run build` from the `site/` directory to ensure all checks pass.\n\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\n*   **Content Format:** Verify if the `content` field expects a raw string, Markdown, or escaped HTML. Adhere to the existing format.\n*   **Character Limit:** Be mindful of the 6000-character limit for the final HTML output as noted in the technical requirements. Brevity is key.\n*   **Date Formatting:** Ensure the date string '2026-04-14' matches the format used by other posts in the array to avoid parsing errors.\n*   **Build Failures:** The `npm run build` command can fail due to TypeScript type errors, linting violations, or syntax errors. It must be run to validate the changes.\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-249 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\nBased on the provided JSON for user story US-249, the task is to create a new blog post for a website, not to implement a feature in a Frappe/Python application. The technical brief below is based on the actual content of the story.\n\n***\n\n**Technical Brief for US-249: Create Gig Economy Blog Post**\n\nThis story involves adding new content to the Pelangi website's blog. All modifications will be within the frontend TypeScript files.\n\n*   **Primary File to Modify:**\n    *   `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`: A new blog post object must be appended to the array of posts.\n\n*   **Involved Components:**\n    *   This change affects the data layer of the blog. No Frappe DocTypes or Python hooks are relevant.\n\n*   **Implementation Approach:**\n    1.  Define a new constant object for the blog post.\n    2.  Populate its properties according to the acceptance criteria:\n        *   `slug`: `gig-jobs-malaysia-waiting-singapore-work-pass`\n        *   `category`: `Career & Work`\n        *   `date`: 